WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.286
<c.p>[Begin Tape 4513.

2
00:00:01.286 --> 00:00:02.571
Begin Session I.]

3
00:00:02.571 --> 00:00:03.000
<v JAMIE DIGILORMO>Alright.

4
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:03.857
Let's see.

5
00:00:03.857 --> 00:00:05.571
Okay, now we're recording.

6
00:00:05.571 --> 00:00:08.143
This is Jamie Digilormo interviewing Mister . . .

7
00:00:08.143 --> 00:00:09.000
<v WESLEY MONTGOMERY>Wes Montgomery.

8
00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:10.286
<v DIGILORMO>Mr. Wes Montgomery.

9
00:00:10.286 --> 00:00:12.000
<v MONTGOMERY>Wes Jones Montgomery.

10
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:15.500
<v DIGILORMO>Here at 1606 Opelousas Street [Lake Charles].

11
00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:16.000
<v MONTGOMERY>Right.

12
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:19.500
<v DIGILORMO>And it is Friday August twenty-eighth, 2015.

13
00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:25.500
So we are here to talk about your experiences in Mossville, Louisiana.

14
00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:32.000
First of all though, I'm going to get some background information on you.

15
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:36.000
So what year, and where, were you born?

16
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.000
<v MONTGOMERY>I was born in Duson, Louisiana.

17
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.000
<v DIGILORMO>Duson, Louisiana.

18
00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.000
I know where that is.

19
00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:43.556
<v MONTGOMERY>Yeah.

20
00:00:43.556 --> 00:00:46.333
And . . . 1934, October the fourth.

21
00:00:46.333 --> 00:00:47.444
<v DIGILORMO>Nineteen thirty-four.

22
00:00:47.444 --> 00:00:51.333
And you say you're eighty years old?

23
00:00:51.333 --> 00:00:52.444
<v MONTGOMERY>I'm eighty.

24
00:00:52.444 --> 00:00:55.778
I'll be eighty-one October the fourth.

25
00:00:55.778 --> 00:00:56.889
<v DIGILORMO>Very nice.

26
00:00:56.889 --> 00:01:03.000
So when . . . So how long did you live in Duson?

27
00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:07.019
<v MONTGOMERY>When I made fourteen I moved here to Lake Charles [Louisiana].

28
00:01:07.019 --> 00:01:07.385
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

29
00:01:07.385 --> 00:01:08.481
<v MONTGOMERY>Well, to Mossville.

30
00:01:08.481 --> 00:01:09.577
<v DIGILORMO>Oh so you . . .

31
00:01:09.577 --> 00:01:11.038
<v MONTGOMERY>Not to Lake Charles.

32
00:01:11.038 --> 00:01:12.500
I moved to Mossville.

33
00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:12.865
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

34
00:01:12.865 --> 00:01:13.596
<v MONTGOMERY>At fourteen.

35
00:01:13.596 --> 00:01:16.154
I moved with my older brother, Valerie.

36
00:01:16.154 --> 00:01:17.250
He's now ninety.

37
00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:17.615
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

38
00:01:17.615 --> 00:01:20.173
<v MONTGOMERY>He's still living, but he's got Alzheimer’s.

39
00:01:20.173 --> 00:01:22.000
I moved with him.

40
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:22.400
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

41
00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:24.800
So your whole family didn't relocate.

42
00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:26.400
Just you and him?

43
00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:30.400
<v MONTGOMERY>No, it was just me, and my brother was here.

44
00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:30.800
<v DIGILORMO>Alright.

45
00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:34.400
So, how many brothers and sisters do you have?

46
00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:37.200
<v MONTGOMERY>It was twelve boys and four girls.

47
00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.400
<v DIGILORMO>So sixteen total?

48
00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:39.200
<v MONTGOMERY>Sixteen total.

49
00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:40.000
<v DIGILORMO>Wow.

50
00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:45.176
<v MONTGOMERY>And we were fifteen of us born in the house with midwives.

51
00:01:45.176 --> 00:01:45.608
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

52
00:01:45.608 --> 00:01:49.922
<v MONTGOMERY>The baby born to the Charity Hospital in Lafayette [Louisiana].

53
00:01:49.922 --> 00:01:50.784
<v DIGILORMO>In Lafayette?

54
00:01:50.784 --> 00:01:51.216
Okay.

55
00:01:51.216 --> 00:01:52.078
<v MONTGOMERY>The baby.

56
00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:53.373
That's just him.

57
00:01:53.373 --> 00:01:56.824
<v DIGILORMO>So what did your parents do in Duson?

58
00:01:56.824 --> 00:01:58.118
<v MONTGOMERY>They were farmers.

59
00:01:58.118 --> 00:01:59.843
They were crop farmers.

60
00:01:59.843 --> 00:02:02.000
Sweet potato, corn, cotton.

61
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:02.345
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

62
00:02:02.345 --> 00:02:04.764
<v MONTGOMERY>That's what they did for their living.

63
00:02:04.764 --> 00:02:05.109
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

64
00:02:05.109 --> 00:02:08.909
<v MONTGOMERY>And my daddy was a . . . He had a gift from Jesus.

65
00:02:08.909 --> 00:02:10.982
My daddy was a faith healer.

66
00:02:10.982 --> 00:02:11.327
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

67
00:02:11.327 --> 00:02:14.091
<v MONTGOMERY>He cured people from all over the world.

68
00:02:14.091 --> 00:02:16.855
<v DIGILORMO>Now would you have called him a traiteur?

69
00:02:16.855 --> 00:02:17.200
<v MONTGOMERY>[Pardon]?

70
00:02:17.200 --> 00:02:19.618
<v DIGILORMO>Would you have called him a traiteur?

71
00:02:19.618 --> 00:02:21.000
Or a treater?

72
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.542
<v MONTGOMERY>He was a treater.

73
00:02:22.542 --> 00:02:23.313
<v DIGILORMO>A treater?

74
00:02:23.313 --> 00:02:23.699
Okay.

75
00:02:23.699 --> 00:02:26.012
<v MONTGOMERY>He was one of the best.

76
00:02:26.012 --> 00:02:29.096
He'd go get them out of the hospital.

77
00:02:29.096 --> 00:02:31.410
That's how powerful this man was.

78
00:02:31.410 --> 00:02:32.181
From God.

79
00:02:32.181 --> 00:02:34.494
He just . . . He worked for Jesus.

80
00:02:34.494 --> 00:02:34.880
<v DIGILORMO>Wow.

81
00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:37.193
Did he use anything to help?

82
00:02:37.193 --> 00:02:41.048
As far as maybe medicinal herbs or anything like that?

83
00:02:41.048 --> 00:02:43.747
Was it just the power of prayer?

84
00:02:43.747 --> 00:02:47.217
<v MONTGOMERY>No. Just the power of God with his hands.

85
00:02:47.217 --> 00:02:49.916
And he had promised me his healing.

86
00:02:49.916 --> 00:02:52.229
He got his from his daddy.

87
00:02:52.229 --> 00:02:53.000
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

88
00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:57.815
<v MONTGOMERY>I was working at Conoco refinery, and he called me one day.

89
00:02:57.815 --> 00:03:01.427
And my daddy never called none of his children.

90
00:03:01.427 --> 00:03:02.631
I was shocked.

91
00:03:02.631 --> 00:03:05.038
He called me up, "Wes, son.

92
00:03:05.038 --> 00:03:07.446
I need you to come home."

93
00:03:07.446 --> 00:03:09.854
So I told my wife Agnes.

94
00:03:09.854 --> 00:03:11.057
My first wife.

95
00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:14.268
I said, "We got to go home Friday.

96
00:03:14.268 --> 00:03:15.873
Meet with my daddy.

97
00:03:15.873 --> 00:03:18.280
I don't know what he want.

98
00:03:18.280 --> 00:03:19.484
He called me."

99
00:03:19.484 --> 00:03:20.688
She said, "Okay."

100
00:03:20.688 --> 00:03:21.892
So we had

101
00:03:21.892 --> 00:03:23.096
<c.p>four little children.

102
00:03:23.096 --> 00:03:24.701
We had four kids.

103
00:03:24.701 --> 00:03:27.911
We had five, but the first one died.

104
00:03:27.911 --> 00:03:29.516
So we had four.

105
00:03:29.516 --> 00:03:31.522
<v DIGILORMO>I'm sorry to hear that.

106
00:03:31.522 --> 00:03:33.127
<v MONTGOMERY>And we come home.

107
00:03:33.127 --> 00:03:37.541
So we got home about nine o’clock, nine-thirty in the morning.

108
00:03:37.541 --> 00:03:40.752
And he had so many cars out there.

109
00:03:40.752 --> 00:03:41.153
People.

110
00:03:41.153 --> 00:03:44.764
So we come in the room where he treat.

111
00:03:44.764 --> 00:03:48.376
He had a room like this with just treating.

112
00:03:48.376 --> 00:03:53.191
Then he had another room about that size where he’d just pray.

113
00:03:53.191 --> 00:03:55.197
You couldn't go in there.

114
00:03:55.197 --> 00:03:56.000
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

115
00:03:56.000 --> 00:03:57.283
<v MONTGOMERY>He just prayed.

116
00:03:57.283 --> 00:04:00.277
So we come in the treating room.

117
00:04:00.277 --> 00:04:04.553
See he grab and hug me and kissed my cheek.

118
00:04:04.553 --> 00:04:10.541
Grabbed my wife kissed her, and he grabbed his four little grandchildren kissed them.

119
00:04:10.541 --> 00:04:11.824
"Wes," he say.

120
00:04:11.824 --> 00:04:13.535
"I'm busy right now.”

121
00:04:13.535 --> 00:04:17.384
He says, "Go in the kitchen, meet your mother."

122
00:04:17.384 --> 00:04:20.805
He called her [May May?] for a nickname.

123
00:04:20.805 --> 00:04:22.943
Her name was Mary Montgomery.

124
00:04:22.943 --> 00:04:25.509
But he called her May May.

125
00:04:25.509 --> 00:04:28.075
He said, "Go meet May May."

126
00:04:28.075 --> 00:04:30.642
And he says, "Sit with her.

127
00:04:30.642 --> 00:04:37.057
About eleven o'clock when I clear all of the crowds out I'll come meet you.

128
00:04:37.057 --> 00:04:39.623
I need to talk to you."

129
00:04:39.623 --> 00:04:42.189
I didn't know what he wanted.

130
00:04:42.189 --> 00:04:43.472
He shocked me.

131
00:04:43.472 --> 00:04:45.610
Knocked me to my knees.

132
00:04:45.610 --> 00:04:49.887
And . . . So about eleven o'clock he done cleared the crowd.

133
00:04:49.887 --> 00:04:51.597
He come in there.

134
00:04:51.597 --> 00:04:59.296
And "Wes," he says, "You know you . . ." He had about ten children one time living in Los Angeles.

135
00:04:59.296 --> 00:05:04.000
He'd go there three times a year and treat people.

136
00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:05.147
<v DIGILORMO>In Los Angeles?

137
00:05:05.147 --> 00:05:05.530
<v MONTGOMERY>Yeah.

138
00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:08.590
Oh, yeah he was all over the world.

139
00:05:08.590 --> 00:05:10.120
"So Wes," he said.

140
00:05:10.120 --> 00:05:13.180
"They want me to pass my treatment down."

141
00:05:13.180 --> 00:05:17.770
But he said, "I don't want to leave it in Los Angeles."

142
00:05:17.770 --> 00:05:21.594
He said, "I want to leave it here in Duson."

143
00:05:21.594 --> 00:05:25.419
And he says, "I talked to your baby sister Diane.

144
00:05:25.419 --> 00:05:27.332
She was my first choice.

145
00:05:27.332 --> 00:05:28.479
She wanted it.

146
00:05:28.479 --> 00:05:31.539
I told her I'd give it to her.

147
00:05:31.539 --> 00:05:34.982
I asked her could she deal with the spirit."

148
00:05:34.982 --> 00:05:36.894
She said, "Oh no Dad."

149
00:05:36.894 --> 00:05:39.954
She said, "No, that I cannot do it."

150
00:05:39.954 --> 00:05:43.014
She said, "I can't deal with no spirit."

151
00:05:43.014 --> 00:05:46.074
So he said, "Wes, I called you up.

152
00:05:46.074 --> 00:05:47.986
Can you deal with spirit?"

153
00:05:47.986 --> 00:05:49.134
"Dad," I said.

154
00:05:49.134 --> 00:05:50.281
"I'm ready today."

155
00:05:50.281 --> 00:05:53.341
He said, "You want to be a healer?"

156
00:05:53.341 --> 00:05:55.253
I said, "I'm ready today."

157
00:05:55.253 --> 00:05:56.401
He said, "Okay.”

158
00:05:56.401 --> 00:06:00.991
He said, “You going to be the next treater in the family."

159
00:06:00.991 --> 00:06:04.051
He says he talk to Agnes my wife.

160
00:06:04.051 --> 00:06:08.641
"Agnes," he say, "You can't be jealous” like my mother May May.

161
00:06:08.641 --> 00:06:10.553
He says, "A jealous woman.

162
00:06:10.553 --> 00:06:12.848
You can't be like that now."

163
00:06:12.848 --> 00:06:17.820
He says, "Wes going to be dealing with people all over the world.

164
00:06:17.820 --> 00:06:19.733
Womens all over the world."

165
00:06:19.733 --> 00:06:23.558
And he said, "They going to be coming in here."

166
00:06:23.558 --> 00:06:27.000
She said, "Dad, what Wes wants I want."

167
00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:29.298
<v DIGILORMO>And what made you so passionate?

168
00:06:29.298 --> 00:06:33.128
What made you say, "I want to do it today"?

169
00:06:33.128 --> 00:06:35.809
<v MONTOGMERY>Because I wanted to be a healer.

170
00:06:35.809 --> 00:06:36.191
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

171
00:06:36.191 --> 00:06:38.106
You wanted to help people?

172
00:06:38.106 --> 00:06:40.404
<v MONTGOMERY>I had been reading the Bible.

173
00:06:40.404 --> 00:06:40.787
Yes.

174
00:06:40.787 --> 00:06:44.234
I wanted to be more powerful than my daddy.

175
00:06:44.234 --> 00:06:45.000
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

176
00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:45.826
<v MONTOMGERY>Oh, yes.

177
00:06:45.826 --> 00:06:51.191
I wanted to give the gift he going to give me from Jesus.

178
00:06:51.191 --> 00:07:01.098
Then I wanted to go back in the Bible and get it some more from Jesus, because I wanted to be huge and powerful.

179
00:07:01.098 --> 00:07:03.162
I wanted to help people.

180
00:07:03.162 --> 00:07:05.226
I wanted to cure people.

181
00:07:05.226 --> 00:07:05.638
Cancer.

182
00:07:05.638 --> 00:07:15.132
I told . . . I believe I could have cured anything if I'd have just . . . If I'd have followed the rules I could cure cancer.

183
00:07:15.132 --> 00:07:20.911
But, I'll admit I had two problem in my life was women and liquor.

184
00:07:20.911 --> 00:07:24.213
And . . . So my daddy died in Los Angeles.

185
00:07:24.213 --> 00:07:27.515
That's where he would treat all the time.

186
00:07:27.515 --> 00:07:32.055
So I did not go to Los Angeles when he died.

187
00:07:32.055 --> 00:07:33.294
I didn't go.

188
00:07:33.294 --> 00:07:38.247
So when he died two of my brothers was at his bedside.

189
00:07:38.247 --> 00:07:41.962
Walter, the one that's one year older than me.

190
00:07:41.962 --> 00:07:43.200
We like twins.

191
00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:46.502
And my brother [Oren?], he's older than us.

192
00:07:46.502 --> 00:07:49.804
Oren died here about six, seven years ago.

193
00:07:49.804 --> 00:07:51.455
But Walter’s still living.

194
00:07:51.455 --> 00:07:55.170
He was here last week with me from California.

195
00:07:55.170 --> 00:07:58.885
So Oren came here and visit me out here.

196
00:07:58.885 --> 00:08:00.123
He told me.

197
00:08:00.123 --> 00:08:03.013
"Wes," he say, "I got my dad."

198
00:08:03.013 --> 00:08:05.489
He say, "You miss Daddy's treatment.

199
00:08:05.489 --> 00:08:08.379
I heard he give it to you."

200
00:08:08.379 --> 00:08:09.617
I said, "Yeah."

201
00:08:09.617 --> 00:08:13.332
But I said, “I wasn't there when he died."

202
00:08:13.332 --> 00:08:15.809
Well he said, "I got it."

203
00:08:15.809 --> 00:08:19.523
But Oren went on he had lied to me.

204
00:08:19.523 --> 00:08:21.174
But I believed him.

205
00:08:21.174 --> 00:08:22.000
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

206
00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:23.135
<v MONTGOMERY>But he lied.

207
00:08:23.135 --> 00:08:25.782
And so here come my other brother.

208
00:08:25.782 --> 00:08:28.430
I call him my twin brother, Walter.

209
00:08:28.430 --> 00:08:31.078
The one who was here last week.

210
00:08:31.078 --> 00:08:36.373
He come here and we went out to, Montgomerys love to party and drink.

211
00:08:36.373 --> 00:08:37.508
We went out.

212
00:08:37.508 --> 00:08:40.534
Have a big time in a night club.

213
00:08:40.534 --> 00:08:40.912
Drank.

214
00:08:40.912 --> 00:08:43.938
Because I had three clubs at one time.

215
00:08:43.938 --> 00:08:47.720
Three night . . . oh, yeah I was . . . That was my problem.

216
00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:51.503
And so we was out partying having a good time.

217
00:08:51.503 --> 00:08:52.637
He said, "Wes."

218
00:08:52.637 --> 00:08:54.528
He said, "You miss Dad's

219
00:08:54.528 --> 00:08:54.907
<c.p>treatment."

220
00:08:54.907 --> 00:08:56.041
I said, "Yeah."

221
00:08:56.041 --> 00:08:59.067
He said, "I tell you what your problem."

222
00:08:59.067 --> 00:09:00.202
I said, "What?"

223
00:09:00.202 --> 00:09:06.254
"Wes," he says, "I ain't never seen nobody in the world that had women like you.

224
00:09:06.254 --> 00:09:07.767
Too many women, Wes.

225
00:09:07.767 --> 00:09:08.523
Women, Wes."

226
00:09:08.523 --> 00:09:11.927
He says, "You got women all over the world."

227
00:09:11.927 --> 00:09:13.440
I said, "Yeah Walter."

228
00:09:13.440 --> 00:09:16.088
I said, "You believe that's what happened?"

229
00:09:16.088 --> 00:09:19.114
He said, "God wouldn't give it to you."

230
00:09:19.114 --> 00:09:23.653
And I knew I was anointed when my mother give me birth.

231
00:09:23.653 --> 00:09:24.788
She had sixteen.

232
00:09:24.788 --> 00:09:29.326
When she got to number seven Jesus told her, "No, that's mine.

233
00:09:29.326 --> 00:09:30.461
I want it."

234
00:09:30.461 --> 00:09:31.596
God anointed me.

235
00:09:31.596 --> 00:09:32.731
I've been anointed.

236
00:09:32.731 --> 00:09:34.244
I'm a blessed man.

237
00:09:34.244 --> 00:09:35.000
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

238
00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:35.787
<v MONTGOMERY>I'm blessed.

239
00:09:35.787 --> 00:09:38.936
It's just these women just took my life.

240
00:09:38.936 --> 00:09:41.298
I was a good looking man.

241
00:09:41.298 --> 00:09:45.234
I had a head of hair like Diamond [Neil Diamond?].

242
00:09:45.234 --> 00:09:48.777
See on my mother's side there are white folks.

243
00:09:48.777 --> 00:09:51.926
And my mom . . . And my daddy the African.

244
00:09:51.926 --> 00:09:55.468
So I came here with just a pretty color.

245
00:09:55.468 --> 00:09:57.043
A head of hair.

246
00:09:57.043 --> 00:09:59.011
Oh, I look like Diamond.

247
00:09:59.011 --> 00:09:59.404
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

248
00:09:59.404 --> 00:10:00.191
<v MONTGOMERY>Six foot.

249
00:10:00.191 --> 00:10:05.309
Weighing about . . . what woman wouldn't want that . . . weighing about a hundred eighty pounds.

250
