<v DIGILORMO>[Laughs] But you owned it.

1221
00:51:56.000 --> 00:51:57.063
<v MONTGOMERY>I owned it.

1222
00:51:57.063 --> 00:51:58.126
It was mine.

1223
00:51:58.126 --> 00:51:58.480
<v DIGILORMO>Wow.

1224
00:51:58.480 --> 00:52:01.669
So you started working at Conoco at what age?

1225
00:52:01.669 --> 00:52:06.630
<v MONTGOMERY>I went to Conoco . . . My mother and daddy had to sign a minor release.

1226
00:52:06.630 --> 00:52:10.173
See at Conoco you had to be twenty-one years old.

1227
00:52:10.173 --> 00:52:14.780
And when I made twenty Conoco called me to go to work then.

1228
00:52:14.780 --> 00:52:17.260
So they didn’t have . . . They just knew.

1229
00:52:17.260 --> 00:52:21.512
They look at a man about two hundred pounds, about six foot.

1230
00:52:21.512 --> 00:52:22.929
Built like a bull.

1231
00:52:22.929 --> 00:52:24.346
And I was built.

1232
00:52:24.346 --> 00:52:26.472
I mean I just was built.

1233
00:52:26.472 --> 00:52:27.535
I had it.

1234
00:52:27.535 --> 00:52:30.370
Had a head of hair looked like Diamond.

1235
00:52:30.370 --> 00:52:33.913
And they brought me in and just took me in.

1236
00:52:33.913 --> 00:52:37.457
<v DIGILORMO>And they knew you because of your work around Mossville?

1237
00:52:37.457 --> 00:52:38.520
<v MONTGOMERY>Yeah, right there . . .

1238
00:52:38.520 --> 00:52:41.000
<v DIGILORMO>They had just seen you around . . .

1239
00:52:41.000 --> 00:52:42.500
<v MONTGOMERY>Yeah Conoco hired me.

1240
00:52:42.500 --> 00:52:47.000
Matter of fact they hadn't hired a black there . . . I made history.

1241
00:52:47.000 --> 00:52:47.375
<v DIGILORMO>Really?

1242
00:52:47.375 --> 00:52:50.750
<v MONTGOMERY>Conoco hadn't hired a black there in ten years.

1243
00:52:50.750 --> 00:52:51.125
<v DIGILORMO>Wow.

1244
00:52:51.125 --> 00:52:53.375
<v MONTGOMERY>I'm the first black they hired.

1245
00:52:53.375 --> 00:52:55.250
I was such a man.

1246
00:52:55.250 --> 00:52:59.000
They didn't want to lose me, so they hired me.

1247
00:52:59.000 --> 00:53:03.125
One day they called me in the office they said, "Wes.

1248
00:53:03.125 --> 00:53:07.250
How old are you?" [coughs] I said, “I'm twenty years old.”

1249
00:53:07.250 --> 00:53:08.375
“Wes," they say.

1250
00:53:08.375 --> 00:53:09.875
"You older than that."

1251
00:53:09.875 --> 00:53:11.750
Said, "What year you born?"

1252
00:53:11.750 --> 00:53:14.000
I said, "1934, October the fourth."

1253
00:53:14.000 --> 00:53:19.250
So Mr. Hank [Clement and Clyde Stuart?] told me, they was the personnel manager.

1254
00:53:19.250 --> 00:53:20.375
"Yeah," they said.

1255
00:53:20.375 --> 00:53:21.875
"That gives you twenty."

1256
00:53:21.875 --> 00:53:23.000
I said, "Yeah."

1257
00:53:23.000 --> 00:53:23.375
"Wes.

1258
00:53:23.375 --> 00:53:26.000
Man, you can’t work here at twenty.

1259
00:53:26.000 --> 00:53:30.875
You got to be twenty when your mother and daddy got to sign."

1260
00:53:30.875 --> 00:53:33.500
I said, "Well they're just like me.

1261
00:53:33.500 --> 00:53:35.375
They can't read and write."

1262
00:53:35.375 --> 00:53:35.750
<v DIGILORMO>[Laughs].

1263
00:53:35.750 --> 00:53:38.375
<v MONTGOMERY>So they gave me some two paper.

1264
00:53:38.375 --> 00:53:42.875
Tell them to just make an X here and an X here.

1265
00:53:42.875 --> 00:53:45.125
“And you can keep your job.

1266
00:53:45.125 --> 00:53:47.000
We won't even dock you.”

1267
00:53:47.000 --> 00:53:48.500
Going to do that.

1268
00:53:48.500 --> 00:53:51.875
I took my car and I went to Duson.

1269
00:53:51.875 --> 00:53:57.875
My mama made an X. My daddy made an X. I brought it back to Conoco.

1270
00:53:57.875 --> 00:54:01.250
I stayed there until I was forty-four years old.

1271
00:54:01.250 --> 00:54:02.000
<v DIGILORMO>Wow.

1272
00:54:02.000 --> 00:54:03.238
<v MONTGOMERY>Worked there twenty-four years.

1273
00:54:03.238 --> 00:54:03.548
<v DIGILORMO>Wow.

1274
00:54:03.548 --> 00:54:04.476
<v MONTGOMERY>Before I quit.

1275
00:54:04.476 --> 00:54:07.571
When I quit I went to go in to business.

1276
00:54:07.571 --> 00:54:08.810
I become a [ . . .?] then.

1277
00:54:08.810 --> 00:54:10.357
<v DIGILORMO>So where is Conoco located?

1278
00:54:10.357 --> 00:54:12.214
Is it in Westlake or is . . .?

1279
00:54:12.214 --> 00:54:13.452
<v MONTGOMERY>On Old Spanish Trail.

1280
00:54:13.452 --> 00:54:15.619
Yeah, in Westlake on Old Spanish Trail.

1281
00:54:15.619 --> 00:54:15.929
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

1282
00:54:15.929 --> 00:54:18.714
Had they just built that whenever you started working?

1283
00:54:18.714 --> 00:54:20.262
Or had it been there . . .?

1284
00:54:20.262 --> 00:54:22.119
<v MONTGOMERY>Oh no, Conoco had been there.

1285
00:54:22.119 --> 00:54:23.667
<v DIGILORMO>It hadn't been there whenever . . .

1286
00:54:23.667 --> 00:54:27.381
<v MONTGOMERY>No, then they build a brand new [Conde Vista?] across the street.

1287
00:54:27.381 --> 00:54:28.000
<v DIGILORMO>Okay

1288
00:54:28.000 --> 00:54:30.019
<v MONTOGMERY>But both of them was Conoco.

1289
00:54:30.019 --> 00:54:34.056
But the plant where I got hired at there was old Conoco.

1290
00:54:34.056 --> 00:54:36.748
No, they were there when I come there.

1291
00:54:36.748 --> 00:54:41.121
<v DIGILORMO>Do you remember how people felt when they started building those plants there?

1292
00:54:41.121 --> 00:54:44.150
I mean what the general feeling was in Mossville?

1293
00:54:44.150 --> 00:54:45.832
Were people glad that there . . .?

1294
00:54:45.832 --> 00:54:48.523
<v MONTGOMERY>Oh, yeah, oh people thought this was it.

1295
00:54:48.523 --> 00:54:50.879
There’s going to be jobs for Mossville.

1296
00:54:50.879 --> 00:54:51.215
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

1297
00:54:51.215 --> 00:54:51.888
<v MONTOGMERY>You see.

1298
00:54:51.888 --> 00:54:55.925
Just like Sasol [energy and chemical company] is coming out there now.

1299
00:54:55.925 --> 00:54:57.944
They want . . . You heard about Sasol?

1300
00:54:57.944 --> 00:54:58.617
<v DIGILORMO>Yes, sir.

1301
00:54:58.617 --> 00:55:03.327
<v MONTGOMERY>Well they want to buy all . . . I own more land than anybody in Mossville.

1302
00:55:03.327 --> 00:55:04.000
<v DIGILORMO>Okay.

1303
00:55:04.000 --> 00:55:05.119
<v MONTGOEMRY>More than anybody.

1304
00:55:05.119 --> 00:55:08.104
So Sasol done called me in a meeting.

1305
00:55:08.104 --> 00:55:11.461
Me and my four children with my first wife.

1306
00:55:11.461 --> 00:55:13.326
They done called me in.

1307
00:55:13.326 --> 00:55:18.176
And they offered me right at a million, but I turned them down.

1308
00:55:18.176 --> 00:55:22.280
I told them, “You got to give me more than that.”

1309
00:55:22.280 --> 00:55:24.891
And my other wife I got now,

1310
00:55:24.891 --> 00:55:30.114
they offer us a hundred and . . . I got a . . . We bought a little house.

1311
00:55:30.114 --> 00:55:31.979
A two bedroom to rent.

1312
00:55:31.979 --> 00:55:33.472
Got it on rent.

1313
00:55:33.472 --> 00:55:38.694
Don't you know they offered me a hundred seventeen thousand for that little house?

1314
00:55:38.694 --> 00:55:40.560
I turned it down, too.

1315
00:55:40.560 --> 00:55:42.798
My wife wanted to sell it.

1316
00:55:42.798 --> 00:55:43.917
My new wife.

1317
00:55:43.917 --> 00:55:44.663
DIGILORMO: Yeah.

1318
00:55:44.663 --> 00:55:46.528
<v MONTGOMERY>I said, "I'm not selling.

1319
00:55:46.528 --> 00:55:51.378
I said, "When I sell they got to have to pay me money."

1320
00:55:51.378 --> 00:55:51.751
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

1321
00:55:51.751 --> 00:55:53.990
<v MONTGOMERY>God gave me all of that.

1322
00:55:53.990 --> 00:55:54.363
<v DIGILORMO>Yeah.

1323
00:55:54.363 --> 00:55:54.736
Right.

1324
00:55:54.736 --> 00:55:58.839
<v MONTGOEMRY>And I says, "God wanted me to buy all this property.

1325
00:55:58.839 --> 00:56:02.197
Why did I buy all this land in Mossville?

1326
00:56:02.197 --> 00:56:03.316
I bought it."

1327
00:56:03.316 --> 00:56:05.927
I said, "God knew Sasol was coming."

1328
00:56:05.927 --> 00:56:08.539
We didn't know, but God know everything.

1329
00:56:08.539 --> 00:56:11.523
"Wes, buy the land, because Sasol is coming.

1330
00:56:11.523 --> 00:56:14.135
You going to be a wealthy man."

1331
00:56:14.135 --> 00:56:14.881
That's right.

1332
00:56:14.881 --> 00:56:16.000
That's God.

1333
00:56:16.000 --> 00:56:19.913
<v DIGILORMO>Well Mr. Montgomery, we been talking for about an hour.

1334
00:56:19.913 --> 00:56:20.304
<v MONTGOMERY>Yeah.

1335
00:56:20.304 --> 00:56:21.870
<v DIGILORMO>That's a long time,

1336
00:56:21.870 --> 00:56:30.087
so would you mind if we maybe . . . I came back in the next week or two and we continue this conversation?

1337
00:56:30.087 --> 00:56:30.478
<v MONTGOMERY>Yeah!

1338
00:56:30.478 --> 00:56:32.435
Anytime you wants to, honey.

1339
00:56:32.435 --> 00:56:34.000
<v DIGILORMO>Great, that's exactly . . .

1340
00:56:34.000 --> 00:56:34.200
<c.p>[End Tape 4513.

1341
00:56:34.000 --> 00:56:34.200
End Session I.]
